.TH NK68_CTL 1 "October 2026" "nk68_ctl" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nk68_ctl \- control Ajazz/NACODEX NK68 keyboard lighting
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nk68_ctl
.B --get
.br
.B nk68_ctl
.B --mode
.I MODE
[options]
.br
.B nk68_ctl
.I MODE SPEED BRIGHTNESS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nk68_ctl
sets or reads the lighting state of an Ajazz/NACODEX NK68 keyboard through
its Linux hidraw configuration interface.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -g ", " --get
Read and print the current lighting state.
.TP
.BR -m ", " --mode " " MODE
Select mode 1 through 13. Mode 13 turns the backlight off.
.TP
.BR -s ", " --speed " " SPEED
Set speed from 1 through 5. The default is 3.
.TP
.BR -b ", " --brightness " " LEVEL
Set brightness from 0 through 5. The default is 5.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Print usage information.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
nk68_ctl --get
nk68_ctl --mode 1 --speed 3 --brightness 5
nk68_ctl 13
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/udev/rules.d/99-nk68.rules
Optional permission rule installed by
.BR make install .
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. Non-zero indicates invalid arguments, an unavailable
device, insufficient permissions, or an HID operation failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR udev(7)
